# what `vercel deploy` must NOT upload from this directory.
#
# scripts/publish-field.sh deploys by running `cd site && vercel deploy --prod`,
# which uploads this directory as it stands — every file in it, not the list in
# $ARTIFACTS. That list names what gets COMMITTED; it has never controlled what
# gets SERVED. https://rabadon.noseydewdrop.com/build.py answers 200 today,
# which is how this was found.
#
# Three things in here carry the operator's absolute home path and none of them
# are part of the site:
#   .rabadon/       this project's own gate state and handoff notes
#   __pycache__/    a .pyc records the absolute path of the source it compiled
#   .env.local      a deploy token
#
# native/publish_redaction_test.sh scans everything under site/ that is NOT
# matched here, so deleting a line from this file does not quietly widen what
# is published — it widens what the test reads, and the test goes red.
.rabadon/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env*
.vercel
